/* 
 * The idea is that a fox shows up and starts watching you, moving closer occasionally. Once it gets close enough, you can give it your catch,
 *  or it might take it from you. This event is mostly flavor, and I wonder if it's worth the complexity. If a dangerous event does trigger, 
 *  the fox will react to it and leave. 
 * Reuses the great hawk rescue event, but I need to test it and think about having the code not be just copy-pasted from its original source. I'll either 
 *  do something different for the rescue, or pull out that great hawk rescue into a shared widget.
 */
:: Fishing Moor Fox Arrive
<<effects>>
<<beastNEWinit 1 fox>>
<<set $daily.fishing.moor.fox.phase to "watching">>
<<set $daily.fishing.moor.fox.closeness to 0>>
<<set $daily.fishing.moor.fox.anger to 0>>

A <<beasttype>> trots out of the heather and stops a short distance away, watching you with bright, curious eyes.<<stress -2>><<lstress>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Fishing Moor Wait]]>><</link>>



:: Fishing Moor Fox Shoo
<<effects>>
You wave the <<beasttype>> away. <<bHe>> skitters back a few paces, crouches, and watches you.
<<set $daily.fishing.moor.fox.closeness -= random(2, 3)>>
<<if $daily.fishing.moor.fox.closeness lt 0>><<set $daily.fishing.moor.fox.closeness to 0>><</if>>
<<set $daily.fishing.moor.fox.anger += random(0, 1)>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Fishing Moor Wait]]>><</link>>


:: Fishing Moor Fox Feed
<<effects>>
<<if $fishingHookedFish.size gte 80>>
	You toss the <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> down in front of the <<beasttype>>. <<bHe>> sniffs it, clamps down, and hauls it off across the moor.
<<else>>
	You toss the <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> to the <<beasttype>>. <<bHe>> catches it neatly and bolts off into the heather.
<</if>>
<<set $daily.fishing.moor.fox.phase to "finished">>
<<unset $fishingHookedFish>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Fishing Moor Wait]]>><</link>>


:: Fishing Moor Fox Angry Feed
<<effects>>
You shove the <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> toward the <<beasttype>>. <<bHe>> snatches it from your hands and bolts off across the moor without looking back.
<<set $daily.fishing.moor.fox.phase to "finished">>
<<unset $fishingHookedFish>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Fishing Moor Wait]]>><</link>>

:: Fishing Moor Fox Molestation
<<if $molestationstart is 1>>
	<<run stopFishingProp()>>
	<<set $molestationstart to 0>>
	<<controlloss>>
	<<violence 1>>
	<<neutral 1>>
	<<molested>>
	<<beastCombatInit>>
	<<endevent>>
	<<set $NPCList[0].stance to "top">>
	<<if $fishingMoorFoxPhase is 2>>
		/* You ate the fish in front of the fox, you monster */
		<<set $enemytrust to -200>>
		<<set $enemyanger to 200>>
	<<else>>
		/* Fox wants fish */
		<<set $enemytrust to -50>>
		<<set $enemyanger to 100>>
	<</if>>
	<<hawkRescueSetup>>
<</if>>

<<effects>>
<<effectsman>>
<<alarmstate>>
<<beast $enemyno>>
<br><br>

<<stateman>>
<br><br>

<<actionsman>>

<<if _combatend>>
	<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Fishing Moor Fox Molestation Finish]]>><</link>></span>
<<else>>
	<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Fishing Moor Fox Molestation]]>><</link>></span>
<</if>>


:: Fishing Moor Fox Molestation Finish
<<effects>>
<<if $enemyarousal gte $enemyarousalmax>>
	<<beastejaculation>>
	The <<beasttype>> pulls back from you, seeming confused. <<bHe>> shakes <<bhis>> head and disappears into the heather.
	<<if $fishingMoorFoxPhase is 1>>
		You stow the <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> safely away.
		<<tending_give $fishingHookedFish.type 1>>
		<<unset $fishingHookedFish>>
	<</if>>
	<<set $daily.fishing.moor.fox.phase to "finished">>
	<br><br>

	<<tearful>> you gather yourself.
	<<clotheson>>
	<<endcombat>>
	<<unset $fishingMoorFoxPhase>>
	<<link [[Return to fishing|Fishing Moor Wait]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Leave|Moor]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><<run stopFishingProp()>><</link>>
<<elseif $alarm is 1 and $rescue is 1>>
	Your cry for help is answered. A <<hawkScreechDesc>> pierces the air. <<hawkRescueApproachSentence>>
	<br><br>

	The <<beasttype>> pulls back at the noise and bolts into the heather.
	<<if $fishingMoorFoxPhase is 1>>
		You manage to hold on to the <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>>.
		<<tending_give $fishingHookedFish.type 1>>
		<<unset $fishingHookedFish>>
	<</if>>
	<<set $daily.fishing.moor.fox.phase to "finished">>
	<<clotheson>>
	<<endcombat>>
	<<unset $fishingMoorFoxPhase>>
	<<npc "Great Hawk">><<person1>>
	<<tearful>> you search the sky. You spot <<if $syndromebird is 1>>your<<else>>a<</if>> <<beasttype>> descending towards you.
	<br><br>

	<<set $phase to 0>>
	<<if $syndromebird is 1>>
		<<link [[Next|Bird Rescue Syndrome]]>><</link>>
	<<else>>
		<<link [[Next|Bird Rescue No Syndrome]]>><</link>>
	<</if>>
	<br>
<<elseif $enemyhealth lte 0>>
	<<beastwound>>
	The <<beasttype>> yelps, backs away with <<bhis>> tail between <<bhis>> legs, then turns and bolts off into the heather.
	<<if $fishingMoorFoxPhase is 1>>
		You stow the <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> safely away.
		<<tending_give $fishingHookedFish.type 1>>
		<<unset $fishingHookedFish>>
	<</if>>
	<<set $daily.fishing.moor.fox.phase to "finished">>
	<br><br>

	<<tearful>> you gather yourself.
	<<clotheson>>
	<<endcombat>>
	<<unset $fishingMoorFoxPhase>>
	<<link [[Return to fishing|Fishing Moor Wait]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Leave|Moor]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><<run stopFishingProp()>><</link>>
<</if>>


:: Fishing Moor Cat Eat Fox
<<effects>>
You glance at the fox, then open wide and drop the whole <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> in your mouth. <<transform cat 1>><<lstress>><<stress -6>>
<<unset $fishingHookedFish>>
<br><br>

The <<beasttype>> stares at you, stunned. Then <<bhis>> expression darkens, <<bhis>> ears go flat, and <<bhe>> launches <<bhimself>> at you.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Fishing Moor Fox Molestation]]>><<set $molestationstart to 1>><<set $fishingMoorFoxPhase to 2>><</link>>


:: Fishing Moor Keep Fox
<<effects>>
<<silently>><<dancedifficulty 1 1000>><</silently>>
<<if $danceSuccess>>
	The <<beasttype>> lunges for your <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> as you unhook it, but you're able to wrench it out of reach just in time.
	<br><br>

	You stow the <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> away, and the <<beasttype>> scampers back, ears flat against <<bhis>> head.
	<<set $daily.fishing.moor.fox.closeness -= random(3, 4)>>
	<<tending_give $fishingHookedFish.type 1>>
	<<unset $fishingHookedFish>>
<<else>>
	As you unhook the <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>>, the <<beasttype>> lunges and snatches it, and scampering off into the heather.
	<<set $daily.fishing.moor.fox.phase to "finished">>
	<<unset $fishingHookedFish>>
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Fishing Moor Wait]]>><</link>>


:: Fishing Moor Throw Back Fox
<<effects>>
<<if dangerEvent()>>
	As you toss the <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> back, the <<beasttype>>'s eyes follow it into the water. <<bHe>> snaps <<bhis>> gaze to you, ears flat. <<bHe>> snarls, then throws <<bhimself>> at you.
	<<unset $fishingHookedFish>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Fishing Moor Fox Molestation]]>><<set $molestationstart to 1>><<set $fishingMoorFoxPhase to 2>><</link>>
<<elseif $rng lt 30>>
	As you throw the <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> back into the water, the <<beasttype>> darts forward and snatches it from the shallows before bounding off into the moor.
	<<set $daily.fishing.moor.fox.phase to "finished">>
	<<unset $fishingHookedFish>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Fishing Moor Wait]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	The <<beasttype>> watches as you throw the <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> back into the water. <<bHis>> shoulders sag and <<bhe>> looks up at you sadly.
	<<unset $fishingHookedFish>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Fishing Moor Wait]]>><</link>>
<</if>>


:: Widgets Fishing Moor Fox [widget]
<<widget "fishingMoorFoxAmbient">>
	<<set _foxMoved to false>>
	<<if $rng gte 50 and $daily.fishing.moor.fox.closeness lt 9 and !$daily.fishing.moor.fox.movedLastLoop>>
		<<set $daily.fishing.moor.fox.closeness += 1>>
		<<set _foxMoved to true>>
	<</if>>
	<<cleareventpool>>
	<<if _foxMoved>>
		<<if $daily.fishing.moor.fox.closeness lte 2>>
			<<addinlineevent 1>>
				The <<beasttype>> pads closer and settles down to watch you.
			<</addinlineevent>>
		<<elseif $daily.fishing.moor.fox.closeness lte 5>>
			<<addinlineevent 1>>
				The <<beasttype>> creeps nearer, crouching low in the heather.
			<</addinlineevent>>
		<<elseif $daily.fishing.moor.fox.closeness lte 7>>
			<<addinlineevent 1>>
				The <<beasttype>> slides closer, settling now only a few paces away.
			<</addinlineevent>>
		<<else>>
			<<addinlineevent 1>>
				The <<beasttype>> slinks to within arm's reach and presses low against the ground.
			<</addinlineevent>>
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		<<if $daily.fishing.moor.fox.closeness lte 2>>
			<<addinlineevent 1>>
				The <<beasttype>> watches you from the edge of the heather.
			<</addinlineevent>>
		<<elseif $daily.fishing.moor.fox.closeness lte 5>>
			<<addinlineevent 1>>
				The <<beasttype>> crouches in the heather nearby, eyes on your float.
			<</addinlineevent>>
		<<elseif $daily.fishing.moor.fox.closeness lte 7>>
			<<addinlineevent 1>>
				The <<beasttype>> sits a few paces away, completely absorbed in watching you.
			<</addinlineevent>>
		<<else>>
			<<addinlineevent 1>>
				The <<beasttype>> lies beside you, motionless, staring intently at your line.
			<</addinlineevent>>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
	<<runeventpool>>
	<<if $daily.fishing.moor.fox.closeness gte 6 and $daily.fishing.moor.fox.anger gte 2>>
		<<if $daily.fishing.moor.fox.closeness lte 7>>
			The <<beasttype>>'s tail twitches and <<bhis>> ears are pinned back.
		<<else>>
			The <<beasttype>>'s ears are flat and <<bhis>> tail is rigid, <<bhis>> body coiled low.
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
	<<set $daily.fishing.moor.fox.movedLastLoop to _foxMoved>>
<</widget>>



/* ========================== */
/* ===== Combat Widgets ===== */
/* ========================== */

<<widget "fishCombatMoorOrgasmFox">>
	<<effects>>
	<<orgasmFishingMoor>>
	The rod slips from your grip. By the time you find your footing again, the line is slack and the <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> is gone. When you recover, you notice that the <<beasttype>> has crept several paces closer while you were distracted.
	<<run endFishingCombat()>>
	<<unset $fishingHookedFish>>
	<br><br>

	<<set $daily.fishing.moor.fox.closeness to Math.min($daily.fishing.moor.fox.closeness + random(2, 5), 9)>>
	<<link [[Next|Fishing Moor Wait]]>><</link>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "fishCombatMoorCaughtFox">>
	<<effects>>
	<<set _canEatFish to canEatFishTf($fishingHookedFish)>>
	<<set _foxLunges to $daily.fishing.moor.fox.closeness gte 8 and $daily.fishing.moor.fox.anger gte random(2, 4)>>
	<<run updateFishRecord($fishingHookedFish.type, $fishingHookedFish.size, "moor")>>
	<<run endFishingCombat()>>
	<<set _fishPropName to "caught-" + $fishingHookedFish.type>>
	<<wearProp _fishPropName>>

	<<fishingCatchFishText "moor">>
	<br><br>

	<<if _foxLunges>>
		But before you can do anything, the <<beasttype>> lunges for the <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>>.
		<br><br>
	<<else>>
		<<if $daily.fishing.moor.fox.closeness gte 8>>
			The <<beasttype>> watches your <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> intently.
			<br><br>
		<<elseif $daily.fishing.moor.fox.closeness gte 7>>
			The <<beasttype>> perks up as you pull out your <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>>.
			<br><br>
		<</if>>

		<<if _canEatFish>>
			It's such a small fish, you could probably fit the whole thing in your mouth, right in front of <<bhim>>.
			<br><br>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>

	<<if _foxLunges>>
		<<link [[Throw the fish at the fox|Fishing Moor Fox Angry Feed]]>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Hold on to the fish|Fishing Moor Fox Molestation]]>><<set $molestationstart to 1>><<set $fishingMoorFoxPhase to 1>><</link>>
	<<else>>
		<<if $daily.fishing.moor.fox.closeness gte 8>>
			<<link [[Stow it away|Fishing Moor Keep Fox]]>><</link>>
		<<else>>
			<<link [[Stow it away|Fishing Moor Keep]]>><</link>>
		<</if>>
		<br>
		<<if $daily.fishing.moor.fox.closeness gte 8>>
			<<link [["Throw the " + $fishingHookedFish.type + " back"|Fishing Moor Throw Back Fox]]>><</link>>
		<<else>>
			<<link [["Throw the " + $fishingHookedFish.type + " back"|Fishing Moor Throw Back]]>><</link>>
		<</if>>
		<<if _canEatFish>>
			<br>
			<<link [[Eat the fish|Fishing Moor Cat Eat Fox]]>><</link>>
		<</if>>

		<<if $daily.fishing.moor.fox.closeness gte 8>>
			<br>
			<<link [["Give the " + $fishingHookedFish.type + " to the fox"|Fishing Moor Fox Feed]]>><</link>>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "fishCombatMoorLineSnappedFox">>
	<<effects>>
	Your line suddenly goes slack, and the <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> disappears into the depths.
	<<run endFishingCombat()>>
	<<unset $fishingHookedFish>>
	<br><br>

	<<switch random(1, 3)>>
		<<case 1>>
			The <<beasttype>> stares at the ripples where the fish was, then looks up at you. <<bHe>> lets out a short huff and lies down, chin on <<bhis>> paws.
		<<case 2>>
			The <<beasttype>>'s ears droop. <<bHe>> watches the water for a moment before looking away, clearly unimpressed.
		<<case 3>>
			The <<beasttype>> sniffs at the water's edge, then turns to look at you with an expression that can only be described as disappointed.
	<</switch>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Re-hook the line and cast back out (0:03)|Fishing Moor Wait]]>><<pass 3>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Leave|Moor]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><<run stopFishingProp()>><</link>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "fishCombatMoorMainFox">>
	<<run fishCombatAction()>>

	/* Handle shoo from previous turn */
	<<if $fishing.moor.playerShooed>>
		<<set $fishing.moor.playerShooed to false>>
		<<set $daily.fishing.moor.fox.closeness to Math.max($daily.fishing.moor.fox.closeness - random(1, 2), 0)>>
		<<set $daily.fishing.moor.fox.anger += 1>>
		You wave the <<beasttype>> back while keeping your grip on the rod. <<bHe>> skitters away a pace or two, ears flat.
		<br><br>
	<</if>>
	<<fishCombatActionDescription>>
	<<printFishInfo>>
	<br><br>

	/* Fox approach countdown, resets each new combat via endFishingCombat clearing $fishing.combat */
	<<set $fishing.combat.foxApproachCountdown ??= random(3, 4)>>
	<<set $fishing.combat.foxApproachCountdown -= 1>>

	<<if $daily.fishing.moor.fox.closeness gte 9>>
		The <<beasttype>> crouches within arm's reach, haunches raised and eyes locked on your line. <<bHis>> entire body is coiled, ready to spring.
	<<elseif $fishing.combat.foxApproachCountdown lte 0>>
		<<set $daily.fishing.moor.fox.closeness to Math.min($daily.fishing.moor.fox.closeness + 1, 9)>>
		<<set $fishing.combat.foxApproachCountdown to random(3, 4)>>
		The <<beasttype>> bounds forward and drops low in the heather, closing the gap between you, <<bhis>> eyes fixed on your line.
	<<elseif $daily.fishing.moor.fox.closeness lte 2>>
		The <<beasttype>> watches from the heather.
	<<elseif $daily.fishing.moor.fox.closeness lte 5>>
		The <<beasttype>> has crept closer, crouching low in the grass and watching your line.
	<<elseif $daily.fishing.moor.fox.closeness lte 7>>
		The <<beasttype>> is only a few paces away now, <<bhis>> gaze fixed on your float.
	<<else>>
		The <<beasttype>> crouches just within arm's reach, watching your line without blinking.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<fishCombatActions "Moor">>
	<<if $daily.fishing.moor.fox.closeness gte 7>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Shoo the fox|Fishing Combat Moor]]>><<set $fishing.moor.playerShooed to true>><<set $fishing.combat.playerAction to "slack">><</link>>
	<</if>>
<</widget>>
